Ladybird’s render side computes a style update beside the event loop,
and the host takes it in later, so two sides each held a walk of the
subtree a hidden element’s styles are cleared from. The host now
clears just the elements the render side’s walk found, so one tree
decides what’s cleared, as it does in the other engines, which compute
style on the main thread from the tree as it is. Blink’s Element::
DetachLayoutTree() clears each element’s style as it detaches the
hidden subtree’s layout tree, and Servo’s clear_descendant_data(),
in Gecko, walks the hidden element’s traversal children and clears
their style data. Chrome 157, Firefox 151, and WebKit 26.5, run with
engine-compare.mjs, all give offsetParent the body and display block
for an element assigned into or out of a slot below an element hidden
a frame before, by the slot attribute, a slot’s name, or assign().
